        {
            "type": "doc_title",
            "bbox": [
                0.042,
                0.478,
                0.755,
                0.625
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "How Boards and CEOs\nCan Build a Shared AI\nVision"
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.043,
                0.657,
                0.226,
                0.676
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "By Judith Wallenstein",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.041,
                0.7,
                0.353,
                0.719
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "ARTICLE JULY 16, 2026 5 MIN READ",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.039,
                0.778,
                0.942,
                0.86
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "There are few topics on which boards and CEOs are better aligned than the urgency of deploying AI in the right way. They agree there's a real risk of moving too late. And they agree there's a danger of investing a lot of money in the wrong areas, losing time and effort in unscalable pilots and use cases, and ending up with no measurable competitive advantage.",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "text",
            "bbox": [
                0.041,
                0.873,
                0.953,
                0.914
            ],
            "angle": 0,
            "content": "Where boards and CEOs often diverge, however, is over the speed, scale, and measurable business impact that AI realistically can be expected to deliver. In our experience, for every board",
            "merge_prev": false
        },
        {
            "type": "footer",
            "bbox": [
                0.044,
                0.969,
                0.25,
                0.985
            ],
            "angle": 0,
